{"version":2,"width":120,"height":40,"timestamp":1795542983,"command":"env DEMO_PAUSE=4 DEMO_CLEAR=1 scripts/demo.sh --tailnet example.ts.net --yes","title":"tailworks launch demo","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[1.764855, "o", "demo on tailnet example.ts.net (apps in /tmp/tw-demo-ts/apps). It will:\r\n  - add tagOwners for the two apps' tags to the tailnet policy (tw policy --apply; additive)\r\n  - add these grants if they are missing:\r\n"]
[2.657439, "o", "      + {\"src\": [\"group:admin\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo-agent\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"]}\r\n      + {\"src\": [\"tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"], \"app\": {\"example.com/cap/mcp\":[{\"limits\":{\"refund\":{\"maxUsd\":50,\"perDayUsd\":200}},\"tools\":[\"lookup_order\",\"refund\"]}]}}\r\n"]
[2.658254, "o", "  - deploy workloads demo (template mcp) and demo-agent (template agent)\r\n"]
[2.658259, "o", "  - take \"refund\" out of the grant tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent → tag:tw-wl-demo for a few seconds, then put it back\r\n"]
[2.658289, "o", "  - kill the agent object it created (demo-095623)\r\nNothing else in the policy is touched. Undo: scripts/demo.sh --tailnet example.ts.net --cleanup\r\n"]
[6.661201, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n\u001b[1m# 1. tailworks is up: one process on this machine, on tailnet example.ts.net\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.661232, "o", "\u001b[1m$ tw status\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.680324, "o", "tw status · /tmp/tw-demo-ts/state · tailnet example.ts.net · mint mode oauth · transport tsnet (loopback through mgmt's node; host embedded in the mgmt process)\r\n"]
[6.680349, "o", "✓ supervisor  pid 58987\r\n✓ node        tw-demo-mgmt-1.example.ts.net (tag:tw-mgmt; API over the tailnet, WhoIs auth) · console https://tw-demo-mgmt-1.example.ts.net/ui/\r\n"]
[6.680366, "o", "✓ mgmt        tenant tn_example · mint queue 0 · 200 registrations/min · 0 warm keys in custody · 0 pending device deletes\r\n✓ host        demo (embedded in the mgmt process) · heartbeat 0.7s ago · objects map[]\r\n✓ internet    Workers direct (Workers' fetch() reaches public internet hosts through this host's network, narrowed by each workload's tailnet.egress.internet)\r\n"]
[6.680368, "o", "  capacity    demo (arm64, no containers) · nodes 0/1000 · vms 0/0 · mem 0/0 MiB (huge 0/0) · vcpu 0/0×0 · scratch 0/0 MiB · 0 containers\r\n"]
[10.686703, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n\u001b[1m# 2. An MCP server and an agent, from the templates (Agents SDK and MCP, unmodified)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.686788, "o", "\u001b[1m$ tw init demo --template mcp\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.700476, "o", "✓ created /tmp/tw-demo-ts/apps/demo from template mcp (workload \"demo\")\r\n"]
[10.70057, "o", "  tags: tag:tw-wl-demo (tw policy prints what to add to your tailnet policy for them)\r\n  cd demo && tw policy && tw deploy   # or `tw dev` for a local run with no tailnet\r\n"]
[10.701553, "o", "\u001b[1m$ tw init demo-agent --template agent\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.714605, "o", "✓ created /tmp/tw-demo-ts/apps/demo-agent from template agent (workload \"demo-agent\")\r\n"]
[10.7147, "o", "  tags: tag:tw-demo-agent-lookup-agent, tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent, tag:tw-wl-demo-agent (tw policy prints what to add to your tailnet policy for them)\r\n  cd demo-agent && tw policy && tw deploy   # or `tw dev` for a local run with no tailnet\r\n"]
[14.722856, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n\u001b[1m# 3. The tailnet policy: the apps' tags, who may call the agent, which tools the agent may call\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.722905, "o", "\u001b[1m$ tw policy demo --apply --yes\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.519244, "o", "tw policy: what demo needs in tenant example.ts.net's tailnet policy (nothing is deployed)\r\n✗ tagOwners  tag:tw-wl-demo: missing (minting its nodes would fail)\r\n? callers    not checked: tailworks doesn't know who you want to allow to call demo\r\n\r\n"]
[15.68339, "o", "› policy     tailworks will add to the tailnet policy (additive: only tag:tw* entries, nothing removed or changed):\r\n    + \"tagOwners\": {\r\n    +   \"tag:tw-wl-demo\": [\"autogroup:admin\",\"tag:tw\"],\r\n    + },\r\n"]
[16.613905, "o", "✓ policy     applied (validated by the control plane; tw audit --all shows it as policy_apply)\r\n  nodes      this app is 1 workload node (TwBudget objects share the workload node); tenant example.ts.net has 0 live nodes (maxObjects 1000; host runs 0 of 1000 node capacity)\r\n\r\nThe policy now has everything tailworks checks; run tw deploy. If people should call demo, make sure a grant like this exists (tailworks didn't write it):\r\n\r\n  \"grants\": [\r\n    { \"src\": [\"autogroup:member\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"] }, // who may call it (not checked: narrow src to a user, group or tag)\r\n  ],\r\n"]
[16.617189, "o", "\u001b[1m$ tw policy demo-agent --apply --yes\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.697815, "o", "tw policy: what demo-agent needs in tenant example.ts.net's tailnet policy (nothing is deployed)\r\n  tags       tag:tw-demo-agent-lookup-agent (the LookupAgent objects' nodes), tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent (the SupportAgent objects' nodes), tag:tw-wl-demo-agent (the workload node)\r\n✗ tagOwners  tag:tw-demo-agent-lookup-agent, tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent, tag:tw-wl-demo-agent: missing (minting its nodes would fail)\r\n? callers    not checked: tailworks doesn't know who you want to allow to call demo-agent\r\n\r\n"]
[16.868401, "o", "› policy     tailworks will add to the tailnet policy (additive: only tag:tw* entries, nothing removed or changed):\r\n    + \"tagOwners\": {\r\n    +   \"tag:tw-demo-agent-lookup-agent\": [\"autogroup:admin\",\"tag:tw\"],\r\n    +   \"tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent\": [\"autogroup:admin\",\"tag:tw\"],\r\n    +   \"tag:tw-wl-demo-agent\": [\"autogroup:admin\",\"tag:tw\"],\r\n    + },\r\n"]
[17.669154, "o", "✓ policy     applied (validated by the control plane; tw audit --all shows it as policy_apply)\r\n  nodes      this app is 1 workload node + 1 node per LookupAgent object + 1 node per SupportAgent object; tenant example.ts.net has 0 live nodes (maxObjects 1000; host runs 0 of 1000 node capacity)\r\n             every node is a device on your tailnet, so your plan's device limit applies (docs/limits.md#tailnet-node-budget)\r\n\r\nThe policy now has everything tailworks checks; run tw deploy. If people should call demo-agent, make sure a grant like this exists (tailworks didn't write it):\r\n\r\n  \"grants\": [\r\n    { \"src\": [\"autogroup:member\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo-agent\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"] }, // who may call it (not checked: narrow src to a user, group or tag)\r\n  ],\r\n"]
[17.672724, "o", "\u001b[2m  tw adds tags, never callers. The two grants of this demo:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.413009, "o", "+ {\"src\": [\"group:admin\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo-agent\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"]}\r\n+ {\"src\": [\"tag:tw-demo-agent-support-agent\"], \"dst\": [\"tag:tw-wl-demo\"], \"ip\": [\"tcp:80\"], \"app\": {\"example.com/cap/mcp\":[{\"limits\":{\"refund\":{\"maxUsd\":50,\"perDayUsd\":200}},\"tools\":[\"lookup_order\",\"refund\"]}]}}\r\n"]
